                    briefing_text_r2:       `Fund the ≈<strong>COP$28.200 millones</strong> across four levers: new bank debt (cheap, control-preserving, eats covenant headroom), equipment leasing (funds the plant off the bank line), retained earnings (a dividend cut), and an outside minority investor (strengthens the balance sheet, dilutes the family). You start at 1,1× EBITDA; every COP$1.000M of new debt adds ~0,08×, and the covenant ceiling is <strong>3,0×</strong>. Sequence the pecking order — <em>don't reach for dilution before exhausting the cheaper levers</em>, and don't fund it all with debt and breach the covenant.`,
